{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Gerrit 1882 PS1 CI diagnosis and immediate remediation: Ubuntu/Python 3.11 failed only tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py::test_all_non_fixture_subprocess_environments_use_the_safe_boundary. The new held-out test constructed child environments by expanding os.environ at lines 51/62, violating the repository safe-repr subprocess boundary; this was a test-harness contract failure, not the bare-targeting behavior. Replaced both raw mappings with tests._subprocess_env.subprocess_env(...) while preserving the exact GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL/GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM controls. The failed guard and held-out oracle now pass together (2/2); lint, typecheck, complexity, hooks, and trailer verification pass. Amended SHA ab425be859 and repushed immediately as PS2; no unchanged recheck."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787100473579501001,"uuid":"b01f0756-f897-45e8-8e07-3e230568cbf2"}